policy "frostphp"
-- frostphp reads source and writes a report. Its whole job is to be the thing
-- that says no, so its own policy grants the least it can and every line here
-- is a decision someone can argue with.

may use filesystem.read      -- reads the files it is asked to analyse
may use filesystem.write     -- writes reports to a stream, and baselines to disk
may use codegen.dynamic      -- $next() and $walk(): a closure and a recursion

forbid the network           -- a linter has no business phoning anywhere
forbid process               -- except the one git diff, suppressed at its call site
forbid deserialize           -- nothing here builds objects from bytes
forbid include.dynamic       -- the only code that runs is the code that shipped
forbid scope                 -- no rewriting variables from data
forbid native                -- stays inside the engine
forbid env.write             -- reads settings, changes none
